106-   The inspection, detention, and removal of aliens who have not been
107-admitted is governed by section 235 of the INA, 8 U.S.C. § 1225. There,
108:Congress defined an applicant for admission as “[a]n alien present in the
109-United States who has not been admitted or who arrives in the United States
110-(whether or not at a designated port of arrival and including an alien who is
111-brought to the United States after having been interdicted in international or
112-United States waters).” INA § 235(a)(1), 8 U.S.C. § 1225(a)(1).
113-
114-    Under section 235, Congress created three different categories of
115-applicants for admission. The first two categories are covered by
116-section 235(b)(1)(A) of the INA, 8 U.S.C. § 1225(b)(1)(A). They include:
