contemporaneous understanding of the statute was the same as
Petitioner’s. See Detention and Removal of Aliens, 62 Fed. Reg. 10312,
10323 (Mar. 6, 1997) (“Despite being applicants for admission, aliens
who are present without having been admitted or paroled . . . will be
eligible for bond and bond redetermination.”).          The government
argues that this regulation shows that the Department of Justice in
