been admitted or paroled” are “applicants for admission,” because
that is what Section 1225(a)(1) deems them to be. But the regulation
clarifies that such noncitizens are still eligible for bond because they
are not also “seeking admission.” It is therefore consistent with
Petitioner’s interpretation of the statute, not the government’s.
